995-01-03/pdf/94-32388.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12944#sec1(c)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 2. Senior Executive Service. Pursuant to section 5382 of title 5, United\nStates Code, the rates of basic pay for senior executives in the Senior\nExecutive Service are set forth on Schedule 4 attached hereto and made\na part hereof.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"60 FR 309, PDF pages 1-10; Sec. 2","sha256":"e9c6f3afe319805c9573be3d5dbd5328bd1551a10d22c63195c41e66ad2c7d55","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1995-01-03/pdf/94-32388.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12944#sec2","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 3. Executive salaries. The rates of pay or salaries for the following\noffices and positions are set forth on the schedules attached hereto and\nmade a part hereof:","original_source":{"page_or_item":"60 FR 309, PDF pages 1-10; Sec. 3 (lead-in)","sha256":"e9c6f3afe319805c9573be3d5dbd5328bd1551a10d22c63195c41e66ad2c7d55","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1995-01-03/pdf/94-32388.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12944#sec3","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) The Executive Schedule (5 U.S.C. 5312–5318) at Schedule 5;","original_source":{"page_or_item":"60 FR 309, PDF pages 1-10; Sec. 3(a)","sha256":"e9c6f3afe319805c9573be3d5dbd5328bd1551a10d22c63195c41e66ad2c7d55","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1995-01-03/pdf/94-32388.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12944#sec3(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) The Vice President (3 U.S.C. 104) and the Congress (2 U.S.C. 31)\nat Schedule 6; and","original_source":{"page_or_item":"60 FR 309, PDF pages 1-10; Sec. 3(b)","sha256":"e9c6f3afe319805c9573be3d5dbd5328bd1551a10d22c63195c41e66ad2c7d55","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1995-01-03/pdf/94-32388.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12944#sec3(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) Justices and judges (28 U.S.C. 5, 44(d), 135, 252, and 461(a)) at Schedule\n7.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"60 FR 309, PDF pages 1-10; Sec. 3(c)","sha256":"e9c6f3afe319805c9573be3d5dbd5328bd1551a10d22c63195c41e66ad2c7d55","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1995-01-03/pdf/94-32388.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12944#sec3(c)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 4. Uniformed services. Pursuant to section 601 of Public Law 103–\n337, the rates of monthly basic pay (37 U.S.C. 203(a)), the rates of basic\nallowances for subsistence (37 U.S.C. 402), the rates of basic allowances\nfor quarters (37 U.S.C. 403(a)) for members of the uniformed services, and\nthe rate of monthly cadet or midshipman pay (37 U.S.C. 203(c)(1), as amended\nby section 601(c) of Public Law 103–337) are set forth on Schedule 8\nattached hereto and made a part hereof.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"60 FR 309, PDF pages 1-10; Sec. 4","sha256":"e9c6f3afe319805c9573be3d5dbd5328bd1551a10d22c63195c41e66ad2c7d55","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1995-01-03/pdf/94-32388.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12944#sec4","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) Pursuant to section 302 of the\nFederal Employees Pay Comparability Act of 1990, as incorporated in section\n529 of Public Law 101–509, employees under statutory pay systems covered\nunder section 1 of this order and members of the United States Park Police\nwho are assigned to a duty station located in one of the geographical areas\nlisted in Schedule 9 shall be entitled, except as may be provided under\nsubsection (b) of this section, to receive an interim geographic adjustment\nat the rate shown on Schedule 9, which is attached hereto and made a\npart hereof.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"60 FR 309, PDF pages 1-10; Sec. 5(a)","sha256":"e9c6f3afe319805c9573be3d5dbd5328bd1551a10d22c63195c41e66ad2c7d55","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1995-01-03/pdf/94-32388.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12944#sec5(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b)(1) The Office of Personnel Management shall prescribe regulations\ngoverning the application of interim geographic adjustments to General\n=== PDF page 2 of 10 ===\n310 Federal Register / Vol. 60, No. 1 / Tuesday, January 3, 1995 / Presidential Documents\nSchedule employees, including the determination of what, if any, geographic\nadjustments shall be payable in the case of employees receiving special\npay rates.\n(2) The Secretary of State shall prescribe regulations governing the applica-\ntion of interim geographic adjustments to employees under the Foreign\nService Schedule, consistent with the regulations and determinations pre-\nscribed under paragraph (1) of this subsection.\n(3) The Secretary of Veterans Affairs shall prescribe regulations governing\nthe application of interim geographic adjustments to employees under the\nschedules for the Veterans Health Administration of the Department of Veter-\nans Affairs, consistent with the regulations and determinations prescribed\nunder paragraph (1) of this subsection.\n(4) The Secretary of the Interior shall prescribe regulations governing\nthe application of interim geographic adjustments to members of the United\nStates Park Police, consistent with the regulations and determinations pre-\nscribed under paragraph (1) of this subsection.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"60 FR 309, PDF pages 1-10; Sec. 5(b)","sha256":"e9c6f3afe319805c9573be3d5dbd5328bd1551a10d22c63195c41e66ad2c7d55","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1995-01-03/pdf/94-32388.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12944#sec5(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) The Office of Personnel Management is hereby designated and empow-\nered to exercise the authority of the President under section 302(c)(1)(D)\nof the Federal Employees Pay Comparability Act of 1990, as incorporated\nin section 529 of Public Law 101–509, to extend the application of interim\ngeographic adjustments shown on Schedule 9, upon the request of an agency\nhead, to employees who would not otherwise be covered.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"60 FR 309, PDF pages 1-10; Sec. 5(c)","sha256":"e9c6f3afe319805c9573be3d5dbd5328bd1551a10d22c63195c41e66ad2c7d55","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1995-01-03/pdf/94-32388.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12944#sec5(c)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 6. Effective dates. The rates of monthly basic pay and allowances\nfor subsistence and quarters for members of the uniformed services provided\nfor at Schedule 8 are effective on January 1, 1995. The other schedules\nprovided for herein are effective on the first day of the first applicable\npay period beginning on or after January 1, 1995.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"60 FR 309, PDF pages 1-10; Sec. 6","sha256":"e9c6f3afe319805c9573be3d5dbd5328bd1551a10d22c63195c41e66ad2c7d55","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1995-01-03/pdf/94-32388.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12944#sec6","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 7. Executive Order No. 12826 of December 30, 1992, and Executive\nOrder No. 12886 of December 23, 1993, are superseded.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"60 FR 309, PDF pages 1-10; Sec. 7","sha256":"e9c6f3afe319805c9573be3d5dbd5328bd1551a10d22c63195c41e66ad2c7d55","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1995-01-03/pdf/94-32388.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12944#sec7","state_at_cutoff":null}],"original_representation":{"page_or_item":"whole per-document Federal Register PDF (60 FR 309)","sha256":"e9c6f3afe319805c9573be3d5dbd5328bd1551a10d22c63195c41e66ad2c7d55","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1995-01-03/pdf/94-32388.pdf"},"research_rationale":"","savings_residuals":null,"schema":"eo-lifecycle-claim/v1","unresolved_material_gaps":["DRAFT: state_at_cutoff not decided for 15 clause(s); clause inventory completeness not confirmed","DRAFT: whole-order ending not established","DRAFT: savings and residual effects not closed","DRAFT: later_source_search not recorded (machine searches are proposals only; paste them after judging them adequate and resolving every CONFLICT line)"],"whole_order_end":null,"whole_order_status":"no"},"draft_schema":"eo-claim-draft/v1","instrument_id":"EO:12944"}
